{
  "_comment": [
    "`paint` is STORAGE ORDER and is APPEND-ONLY. A pixel is persisted as its index in this",
    "array (1-based; 0 is the eraser), so reordering or inserting anything before the end",
    "silently recolours every pixel already on the shared canvas. New colours go at the END.",
    "A colour's HEX may be retuned in place - the pixel keeps its index and simply renders in",
    "the new shade - which is how the palette moved onto the official wplace colours in v1.2.",
    "Two indices MAY share a hex (older colours that retuned onto the same wplace shade);",
    "storage keeps both so old art still renders, and `displayOrder` shows each shade once.",
    "`displayOrder` is what the palette shows, and may be rearranged freely - it is a list of",
    "names, not indices. mg_pixelbattle_palette_test.js enforces all of this."
  ],
